  "instructions": "SKILL verify-wow-client (.agents/skills/verify-wow-client/SKILL.md)\n---\nname: verify-wow-client\ndescription: Validar uma funcionalidade de addon no cliente real do WoW Forever, reproduzir falhas e registrar evidência com escopo e limites.\n---\n\n# verify-wow-client\n\nUse ao planejar a prova de utilidade e ao testar uma candidata no jogo. Leia os casos factuais em [lições](../../../knowledge/seed-docs/forever-live-client-lessons.md) a partir da raiz do repositório; o caminho canônico é knowledge/seed-docs/forever-live-client-lessons.md.\n\n- Defina antes do código o resultado visível e a transição real que o demonstram. Um modo demonstração comprova desenho, não detecção. Separe coleta → associação/decisão → desenho → recuperação para localizar falhas.\n- Registre build/interface, versão e contexto (mapa/instância, combate, quest/alvo). Compare os arquivos instalados com o candidato; recarregue após alterações. Instalações paralelas ou scripts antigos podem invalidar o diagnóstico.\n- Observe primeiro o estado e os contadores; consulte apenas as APIs indispensáveis. Se um valor é secreto, descarte-o antes de comparar, formatar ou extrair partes. pcall não transforma valor secreto em público. Não atribua causa sem a leitura real que a sustenta.\n- Use os controles e comandos do próprio addon para configurar/diagnosticar. Quando uma consulta de leitura exigir confirmação de scripts do cliente, o usuário resolve o aviso; não automatize a confirmação nem contorne a restrição.\n- Siga a autorização de movimento do usuário e a ferramenta de controle disponível. Captura antiga não autoriza clique: reobserve após reload, troca de janela ou entrada concorrente; não digite comandos sem confirmar o foco do chat. Não fixe IDs de janela, coordenadas da tela ou personagens nesta skill.\n- Reproduza o problema, aplique uma correção focal e repita o mesmo cenário. Acrescente uma regressão do comportamento que o mock não cobria. Depois rode os checks da fábrica e confira o conteúdo final instalado/empacotado.\n- Registre ações realmente observadas e pendências em relatório por cenário. PARTIAL_CLIENT_TESTED é uma descrição de escopo, não promoção dos metadados globais clientVerified. Ausência de erro visível não prova ausência de taint. Não declare quests/combate/instâncias testados por analogia.\n- Preserve somente recortes relevantes e sem chat/dados de terceiros como evidência de produto. Rotule mocks. Deixe opções e personagem em estado seguro e documentado.\n\nEvidências originais: research/AURANPC/LIVE-SESSION-2026-11-16.md; research/AllianceDungeonTrail/LIVE-TEST.md. A sessão antiga não autoriza controle de um jogo em uma tarefa futura.\n\nFaction coverage: new/revised addons support Alliance and Horde. Plan and record acceptance separately for both, including unknown faction and reload/character changes. Shared rendering/API lessons may be reused; historical Alliance observations do not certify Horde quests, routing or live behavior. Apply docs/FACTION-SUPPORT.md.\n\n## Item objectives and installed artifacts (70959, 2026-11-18)\n\n- An active required item can have questID=nil and isActive=false, and no QuestTitle tooltip line. Compare a public exact ItemName with current public item objectives; do not equate generic quest classification with an active quest. Preserve unknown/secret handling and remove stale matches after quest changes. Regress with the actual observed fields, not idealized questID fixtures only.\n- Install the generated addons directory/ZIP, including its injected branding TOC. Source TOCs omit generated modules by design. Compare installed Lua/TOC hashes to the generated artifact before interpreting failures.\n- Auto-loot may hide the window before visual inspection. Temporarily change the setting only for testing, restore it and verify. Test collection and cleanup as well as appearance. If item deletion also abandons a quest, record the consequence before proceeding.\n- Scoped evidence: research/AURANPC/LIVE-SESSION-2026-11-18.md (Alliance, ptBR, open world only).\n\n\nSKILL publish-wow-addon (.agents/skills/publish-wow-addon/SKILL.md)\n---\nname: publish-wow-addon\ndescription: Prepare a tested WoW addon for public distribution, benchmark it in the client, create accurate CurseForge materials and record publication status. Use for release/deploy requests, not ordinary feature edits.\n---\n# Publish a WoW addon\n\nApply the repository build workflow and preserve the approved gameplay behavior. Read products/TonhoQuestGlow/DEPLOYMENT-CONTEXT.md for the original scoped example, not as proof for another release.\n\n- Separate the installable product from engineering records. Use distribution: public through the validated packager; never hand-remove validation requirements. Public packaging still runs product/faction tests and stores build evidence outside the ZIP. Keep runtime, assets, user instructions and mandatory license notices; exclude blueprints, reports, caches, absolute user paths, credentials and build logs. Do not obfuscate Lua or remove required attribution to hide implementation history.\n- When renaming, distinguish display title, installation folder/TOC, frames, commands, asset paths and SavedVariables. Retain useful aliases and document profile migration. Avoid two enabled renderers. Check whether the client discovers the new folder after reload; do not present old-folder testing as proof of the final installation identity.\n- Benchmark with the client's available APIs. Record build, addon identity/version, locale, visible plates, open windows, sample intervals and raw measurements. GetAddOnMemoryUsage after UpdateAddOnMemoryUsage measures attributed addon memory; it is not process RAM, GPU texture memory or proof of a leak. FPS is contextual, not a causal addon cost. Compare cold/warm and representative UI states; only optimize a demonstrated cost, preserve every feature and retest the same scenarios. Document profiler overhead, interruptions and unavailable metrics. Do not ship temporary benchmark instrumentation or automate anti-AFK behavior in the addon.\n- Keep the character safe and active only within the current user's authorization. Reobserve after focus changes. Bound tool calls; after a helper stall, reset/reselect from inventory and verify login/combat before resuming. Never claim uninterrupted observation across a stalled control session.\n- Recheck current official CurseForge requirements. Prepare English-first description, truthful compatibility/version tags, original400x400 PNG icon, actual installation ZIP, changelog, categories, license, commands and support channel. Additional languages may follow English. Do not tag another game flavor to bypass a missing correct version.\n- Use actual screenshots where available, crop private chat/player names, and identify any reconstruction or AI-modified showcase. Never invent a captured game state. Keep a manifest linking image, scene, version and allowed crop.\n- Publishing requires current authorization and a logged-in author account. Login/CAPTCHA/agreements may require user handoff. An open desktop CurseForge app does not imply an authenticated author portal. Keep READY, SUBMITTED, UNDER_REVIEW and PUBLISHED separate; record IDs/URLs only after visible confirmation. Do not call a local ZIP deployed to CurseForge. If blocked, finish the upload kit and report the exact remaining step.\n- For long portal text, prefer paste/fill and verify the full content: character-by-character typing can time out halfway. For uploads use the documented filechooser flow before clicking the visible file button; if a logo chooser fails, a later ZIP/media chooser may still work. Check the resulting filename/version/status rather than assuming a click uploaded it.\n- Open the repository PR and verify Actions; no automatic merge. Save concise release context, benchmark methodology and limits; index original lessons into RAG, regenerate changed local vectors and check retrieval. Do not store account sessions, tokens or private logs in the knowledge base.\n"
